":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/f439fab4927f2793216ae1be64fd06400e2cb92a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/f413a71d5401918fb46423e20a3bfd9cb2660652.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/385d5218f85f256844b9a55e28cdd1b0d6af3864.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/b04524e884a92191767420164a9c5ddd77590310.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ec0192a5b72f64de4f46bb654fecb06a17d66a22.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"multi | Marks +1"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A random variable x has the following probability distribution:<br /><img src=\"/media/1db0418ae9dc64e9930c5b0d982c486642689eb6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.02","high":"1.11"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/6b7601b5d9d8d7653340ee798af23e0ca2afb475.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Three numbers are chosen at random without replacement from {1, 2, _ _ _ _ 10}. The probability that the minimum of the chosen number is 3 or their maximum is 7, is _____.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.25","high":"0.3"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/687c64d5c4e8cf107299bb16211ca31beecb3820.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/3d74c34aa86d524e76d1d7e25ba4522b3d14e102.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The random variable x take on the values 1, 2 or 3 with probabilities<br /><img src=\"/media/b9d4c5569f9acec3743fd2d83c19c4b21be47af1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /><br />respectively. The value of <em>P </em>and <em>E</em>(<em>x</em>) are respectively</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>0.05, 1.87</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>1.90, 5.87</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>0.05, 1.10</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0.25, 1.40</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/663d5d456bdf5a6a25b26bbdbc571394d35aa4a7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>How many 3-digit numbers can be formed using three distinct single digit prime numbers?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>64</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>24</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>12</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>4</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>The set of single-digit prime numbers is {2, 3, 5, 7}.<br />The number of ways to select 3 digits out of 4 is 4.<br />The number of ways to arrange them to form a 3-digit number = 3! = 6<br />Total possible 3 digit numbers = Number of ways to select &times; Ways to arrange<br /> = 4 &times; 6 = 24</p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/217f2b2ad212a0ee00af2be1049e53c275d3fc08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/0b0f1dcea73a9347c79534c237143b288d0d7c3a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/e0b8fb2d918b04e25f0ad7fa19ff8947a7486609.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/c1c79783654608c03fd04d67d9b5fcd306c0412f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/9d04aa223fd516a7b1f36559f516bc4b6c3a